{% comment %}
  The ring sizer, in the footer's Support column, next to the size guide it complements.

  noritamy.com copy of the IL block: English only, and it renders nothing until a page with the
  handle "ring-sizer" exists (template "ring-sizer"), so the footer never links to a 404.

  A custom block rather than one more of the theme's `text` blocks, for two reasons.

  The footer's text blocks hold English in the template and render Hebrew on the storefront
  through Shopify's stored translations. A new text block has no translation, so it would have
  shown "Measure your ring size" in the middle of a Hebrew column. This picks its own language.

  And phones only, the same rule as the other two entry points. A monitor cannot be calibrated,
  so on a desktop the link would lead to a page whose only message is "open this on your phone".
  The size guide link directly above it is the right answer there and stays for everyone. The
  block ships hidden so a desktop never sees it flash.

  One root element, with the style and the script inside it. The theme wraps each block in its
  own container, and keeping everything in one node means the block behaves like any other.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  # routes.root_url is "/" on the primary locale and "/he-il" on the others, with no trailing
  # slash, so appending and then collapsing the double slash is the only join right in both.
  assign rs_url = routes.root_url | append: '/pages/ring-sizer' | replace: '//', '/'
  assign rs_text = 'Measure your ring size'
  assign rs_page = pages['ring-sizer']
-%}

{%- if rs_page.url != blank or request.design_mode -%}
<div class="rs-footer-link" hidden {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <p><a href="{{ rs_url }}" title="{{ rs_text | escape }}">{{ rs_text }}</a></p>

  <style>
    .rs-footer-link[hidden] { display: none !important; }
    .rs-footer-link p { margin: 0; }
    /* 14px to sit level with the links above and below it. The theme renders those through a
       generated per-block class that a custom block cannot reuse, and the column itself
       inherits 17px, so the size has to be stated rather than inherited. */
    .rs-footer-link a { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }
  </style>

  <script>
    (function () {
      /* The same three signals the product page and the guide page use, so no entry point can
         disagree with another about what counts as a phone: a coarse pointer AND a touch
         digitiser AND a short edge of phone proportions. A touchscreen laptop clears the first
         two and fails the third, and a desktop browser narrowed to a phone width still reports
         the real screen. */
      var coarse = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches;
      var touch = (navigator.maxTouchPoints || 0) > 0;
      if (!(coarse && touch && Math.min(screen.width, screen.height) <= 520)) return;
      var all = document.querySelectorAll('.rs-footer-link[hidden]');
      for (var i = 0; i < all.length; i++) all[i].hidden = false;
    })();
  </script>
</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Ring sizer link",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Ring sizer link" }]
}
{% endschema %}
